kers to say to the American  diplomats but you know that is the  reality but the second thing is that one  of my one of my staff noticed that there  were barcoding  on the trays the big tub plastic tubs of  shrimp  and they were you know hitting it with  the bar cutting machine and she asked  what what's going on they're like oh we  have to do that because the American  Food and Drug association or Food and  Drug Administration requires us to be  able to know where the shrimp came from  in case there's a health outbreak these  are the same companies in a country  where the government and the companies  had been telling us oh we can't trace  this back to the actual vote it's like  they didn't want to trace it back to the  actual  for this purpose hmm the question that  that raises to me though is why doesn't  the United States Food and Drug  Administration has the power to look at  that then why doesn't the Customs and  Border Protection have the power to do  that so that we don't bring in slaves  made goods and so as a result President  Obama issued an executive order doing  just that  and we were able to get with Senator Ron  Wyden and others a change to the tariff  act that made it clear that you couldn't  import slave named Goods and so now  tracing down to the boat tracing down to  the farm and actually requiring that  they look at their supply chain if they  expect to bring things in the United  States that's becoming a reality  and we are very happy to see actually  that one of the people from US Customs  and Border Protection one of the folks  who's setting up that office and is  gonna be doing the frontline work  actually came up to the GL see what  works conference which you know I think  that that's when you're putting on an  academic conference and suddenly field  practitioners start showing up you know  I think it shows that you're really on  the right track right well thank you so  much for being here today and sharing  some of your work and we'll look 